    "increase": "Add {value} for {team}",
    "decrease": "Remove {value} for {team}",
    "info": "Allowed scores: <b>2 to 155, or 257 for a match</b>. Entering 257 gives the other team <b>0 points</b> and automatically counts one match. Otherwise: <b>157 − entered score</b>. In 1500 mode, the total is doubled once.",
    "help_start_title": "Start",
    "help_start_body": "Choose 1000 points or 1500 (♠ ♠: points and announcements doubled). If the trump guide is enabled, choose the starting team when you first tap points or announcements. Trumps then alternate after each round. In Menu → Options, toggle the trump guide and round numbers on the slate: ✓ on, ✕ off.",
    "help_scores_title": "Enter a round",
    "help_scores_body": "Enter 2 to 155 for either team: the other receives 157 minus that number. Match records 257 against 0 and is not an announcement. Announcement counters reset after the round; earned points remain credited. The sheet and slate share scores. On the slate, tap the black area to enter points.",
    "help_order_title": "Fill in rounds in order",
    "help_order_body": "Only the first empty row is available. Later rows stay grey until the preceding row is filled in. Completed rows can still be edited. To correct a round, change one field. To clear it, empty one field and confirm: that round and all later rounds are cleared to keep the rounds in order. If correcting the last round reaches or exceeds 1000 points, or 1500 in double spades mode, the winner panel appears again even if it was previously closed. This applies to both the score sheet and the slate.",
    "help_match_title": "Count a match",
    "help_match_body": "257 gives the other team 0 and adds one match to the counter. If a team wins all the points in a round, enter 257, not 157. The + next to “Match” enters 257 on the next empty row. The − removes that team’s last match and clears its round and all later rounds. Editing or clearing a 257 updates the counter. The 257 points are included in the round scores and are not added again as melds.",
    "help_ann_title": "Announcements before points",
    "help_ann_body": "20 points = 3 cards; 50 = 4 cards; 100 = 5 cards or four of a kind; 150 = four nines; 200 = four jacks. Use + and −, or M on the slate, then OK. Announcements give opponents no points. On desktop, announcement boxes show only the heading; on phones, they also show the team name.",
    "help_finish_title": "Win",
    "help_finish_body": "The first team to reach or exceed the target wins, including through announcements before a round. New entries are then blocked. Close the panel with × to correct the last round if needed. New game saves the result and resets scores.",
    "help_history_title": "View game history",
    "help_history_body": "“History” shows games, dates, teams, scores, mode, meld points and the match counter. Older games without a saved match counter show “—”. The winner is the first team to reach the target. A game stopped before the target has no winner. If the winner was not saved, “Winner not recorded” is shown. The cross deletes one game after confirmation; “Clear history” deletes all games after confirmation. The icon below the cross shares a summary with scores, melds and match counts; if sharing is unavailable, you can copy it. Games played on the slate are saved in the same history when you confirm “New game”, labelled “Slate game”. “History” on the slate opens the list, and “Back to the game” returns to the slate.",
    "help_save_title": "Saving, sharing and printing",
    "help_save_body": "The current game and history are saved in this device’s browser, without syncing to other devices. Clearing browser data may delete these saved games. Sharing next to the title shares or copies the application’s address, without sharing saved games. “Slate” opens the full-screen slate; “Print history” prints the displayed games.",
    "help_install_title": "Language, phone and storage",
    "help_install_body": "The menu to the right of Share provides language selection: ⋮ on phones, Menu on desktop. Language offers Français, Deutsch, Italiano, Rumantsch and English. The flag beside the title is decorative. Android: Chrome menu → Install / Add to Home screen. iPhone: Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen. After fully loading the HTTPS site once online, the game works offline. Saves stay in this browser; clearing browser data may delete them. On desktop, Menu is to the right of History. On phones, Share in the menu lets you send the application link. On phones, tap Language in the menu to show the available languages.",
    "help_language_title": "Choose a language",
